      <section class="c-sec" id="where-they-differ">
        <h2>Where they differ</h2>
        <ul class="c-dots">
          <li><b>Free plan.</b> Everfit lists its Starter plan as free for up to 5 clients. Trainerize lists a free plan for 1 client.</li>
          <li><b>Plan steps.</b> Everfit prices Pro from 5 to 300 clients and Studio from 50 to 500. Trainerize's Grow plan covers 2 clients, Pro runs from 5 to 200, and Studio Plus starts at 500.</li>
          <li><b>AI replies.</b> Everfit bills Smart Response per coach in credits, with 50 free credits a month on eligible paid plans, as a subscription separate from the workspace plan. Trainerize sells FitMetrics as a paid add-on. Everfit's drafts draw on the coach's Knowledge Base and Saved Responses; Trainerize says FitMetrics learns from a linked website or uploaded Q&amp;A knowledge base and from conversation history.</li>
          <li><b>Branding.</b> Everfit lists Custom Branding on Pro and Studio and sells Advanced Custom Branding for a one-time $75. Trainerize lists a one-time $169 setup fee for its branded app on Pro and includes a branded app in Studio Plus.</li>
          <li><b>Payments.</b> Everfit lists its Payments &amp; Packages add-on from $9 per month. Trainerize lists its Stripe add-on at $10 USD per month on Grow and Pro and includes it in Studio Plus.</li>
          <li><b>Exercise library.</b> Everfit lists 1,000+ exercises and creating your own on all plans. Trainerize lists over 2,100 filmed exercises and says coaches can upload their own exercise videos.</li>
          <li><b>Add-ons.</b> Everfit sells Autoflow, On-Demand Collections, Meal Plans &amp; Recipe Books and Payments &amp; Packages as add-ons, and includes On-Demand Collections in Studio. Trainerize sells Advanced Nutrition Coaching, Business, Video Coaching and Stripe payments as add-ons on Grow and Pro, and lists those four as included in Studio Plus; FitMetrics is a separate paid add-on.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="c-sec" id="what-they-have-in-common">
        <h2>What they have in common</h2>
        <p>Both list a free plan, a 30-day free trial with no card required, an AI workout builder, AI reply drafts for the coach to review (Trainerize says review is the default), AI that draws on material the coach supplies, branded app options, payments through Stripe, Zapier, wearable integrations including Apple Health, Google Health, Garmin and Fitbit, and an exercise library with a way to add your own exercises.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="c-sec" id="everfit-in-more-detail">
        <h2>Everfit in more detail</h2>
        <p>Everfit lists a free Starter plan for up to 5 clients. Pro runs from $19 per month for 5 clients to $290 per month for 300 clients on monthly billing, and Studio runs from $105 per month for 50 clients to $430 per month for 500 clients. Its exercise library lists 1,000+ exercises, and coaches can create their own with custom videos on every plan.</p>
        <p>Everfit lists an AI Workout Builder that turns notes or PDFs into a program, and Smart Response, which Everfit describes as <a href="https://everfit.io/ai-suite/" rel="noopener">"AI-drafted replies in your voice"</a> that coaches "just review, edit, and send." Its <a href="https://help.everfit.io/en/articles/13212021-ai-smart-response" rel="noopener">help center</a> says drafts are based on the current chat context and can draw on the coach's Knowledge Base and Saved Responses. Smart Response is <a href="https://help.everfit.io/en/articles/16881431-ai-smart-response-credits-and-plans" rel="noopener">credit based and billed per coach</a>: each coach on an eligible paid plan gets 50 free credits per month, and a paid seat, assigned to a specific coach, gives that coach 250, 1,200 or 3,500 credits per month instead, for $15, $50 or $100 per month. Everfit says Smart Response is not available on Trial or Starter workspaces.</p>
        <p>Everfit's <a href="https://everfit.io/integration/" rel="noopener">integrations page</a> names Apple Health, Google Health, Apple Watch, Garmin, Fitbit, WHOOP, Oura, MyFitnessPal, Cronometer, Stripe and Zapier. Its help center says Zapier is available <a href="https://help.everfit.io/en/articles/8543585-introducing-zapier-integration" rel="noopener">"as a Plugin on the Studio plan"</a>. Payments are an add-on, and Everfit's <a href="https://help.everfit.io/en/articles/5684968-processing-fees-for-payments" rel="noopener">payment fees page</a> says the platform fee for using it is USD $9 per month. Everfit lists Custom Branding on Pro and Studio, and its <a href="https://help.everfit.io/en/articles/5754312-advanced-custom-branding-bring-your-brand-to-the-next-level" rel="noopener">help center</a> lists Advanced Custom Branding as a $75 one-time add-on for Pro and Studio and points coaches who want their own app listings to its white-label solution on Enterprise.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="c-sec" id="trainerize-in-more-detail">
        <h2>Trainerize in more detail</h2>
        <p>Trainerize has been part of ABC Fitness since September 2020, according to its <a href="https://www.trainerize.com/about/" rel="noopener">About page</a>. It lists a free plan for 1 client, a 30-day free trial with unlimited clients, and paid plans priced by number of clients, from Grow (2 clients) through Pro to Studio Plus, with a 10% discount for annual billing.</p>
        <p>Its AI Workout Builder is included from the Grow plan up. FitMetrics, which Trainerize calls <a href="https://www.trainerize.com/blog/ai-coaching-software-with-coach-control/" rel="noopener">"a new AI add-on"</a>, drafts check-in replies from a client's logged data. Trainerize's <a href="https://www.trainerize.com/features/fitmetrics/" rel="noopener">FitMetrics page</a> says coaches can "Link your website or upload your own Q&amp;A knowledge base" so that the AI "learns your approach and tone so its drafts sound like you", and that "By default, you review every drafted reply before anything sends to a client."</p>
        <p>FitMetrics is a paid add-on. Trainerize's public pages currently describe FitMetrics pricing differently, so this page does not state a FitMetrics price. Check <a href="https://www.trainerize.com/features/fitmetrics/" rel="noopener">Trainerize</a> for current pricing.</p>
        <p>Trainerize's <a href="https://www.trainerize.com/integrations/" rel="noopener">integrations page</a> lists Apple Health, Google Health, the Apple Watch app, Garmin, Fitbit, Withings and MyFitnessPal, says Google Health Connect brings in data from apps "including Oura, Samsung Health, WHOOP, and others", and says its Mindbody, ABC Glofox and ABC Ignite integrations are "available only for Studio or Enterprise plans". The FitMetrics page says WHOOP and Oura "integrate directly" and that FitMetrics supports API and MCP access to connect tools such as Claude or ChatGPT to a coach's Trainerize data. Its <a href="https://www.trainerize.com/pricing/" rel="noopener">pricing page</a> lists Stripe Integrated Payments as a $10 USD per month add-on on Grow and Pro, and a custom branded app for a one-time $169 setup fee on Pro, and its Studio Plus card lists Advanced Nutrition Coaching, Business, Video Coaching and Stripe Integrated Payments as included. Its About page describes a library of over 2,100 professionally filmed exercises, and its <a href="https://resources.trainerize.com/faq" rel="noopener">FAQ</a> says coaches can upload their own exercise videos.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="c-sec" id="questions-to-settle-before-you-choose">
        <h2>Questions to settle before you choose</h2>
        <ul class="c-dots">
          <li><b>Clients now and next year.</b> Where your client count falls in each company's plan steps, today and as you grow.</li>
          <li><b>AI replies.</b> Whether you want them, what you would give the AI to learn from, how you review drafts, and how they are billed: per coach in credits, or as an add-on.</li>
          <li><b>Branding.</b> Custom branding inside the company's app or your own app-store listing, which plan includes it, and any fee.</li>
          <li><b>Payments.</b> Built in or an add-on, and each company's current processing fees.</li>
          <li><b>Integrations.</b> The wearables, nutrition apps and automation tools you already use.</li>
          <li><b>Nutrition, booking and on-demand content.</b> Whether each is in the plan you would buy or an add-on, and at what price.</li>
          <li><b>Trial.</b> What the trial includes. Everfit says Smart Response is not available on trial workspaces, and Trainerize says add-ons are not included in its trial.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="c-sec" id="where-wolvec-fits">
        <h2>Where Wolvec fits</h2>
        <p>Wolvec is an AI platform for fitness coaches and online personal trainers, the whole coaching setup rather than an add-on to it. Your AI is built from one conversation about how you coach, so you can start without a content library.</p>
        <p>Depending on the chat level you choose, your AI can answer routine questions based on how you coach, draft a reply for you to review, or stay off. The catalog comes with animated demos and step-by-step instructions, so you are not filming or writing them up yourself.</p>
        <p>Some of this overlaps with Everfit and Trainerize: both list AI reply drafts for the coach to review, both describe AI that draws on material the coach supplies, and both list exercise libraries. Both also publish pricing and list free plans, trials, payments, branded apps and integrations, which this page does not cover for Wolvec. Wolvec does not currently publish pricing, and this page makes no statement about whether any Wolvec feature is included in a base price or carries a separate charge.</p>
        <p>Wolvec is in early access by invitation. For more options, see <a href="/compare/trainerize-alternatives">Trainerize alternatives for fitness coaches</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="c-sec" id="frequently-asked-questions">
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <div class="c-faq">
        <div class="c-faq-item">
          <h3>Is Everfit or Trainerize free?</h3>
          <p>Both list a free plan. Everfit's Starter plan is free for up to 5 clients, and Trainerize's free plan covers 1 client. Both also list a 30-day free trial with no card required.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="c-faq-item">
          <h3>How do Everfit and Trainerize charge for AI replies?</h3>
          <p>Everfit bills Smart Response per coach in credits, as a subscription separate from the workspace plan, with 50 free credits a month on eligible paid plans. Trainerize sells FitMetrics as a paid add-on. Trainerize's public pages currently describe FitMetrics pricing differently, so this page does not state a FitMetrics price. Check Trainerize for current pricing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="c-faq-item">
          <h3>Do Everfit and Trainerize let the coach review AI replies?</h3>
          <p>Everfit says coaches review and edit Smart Response drafts before sending. Trainerize's FitMetrics page says "By default, you review every drafted reply before anything sends to a client."</p>
        </div>
        <div class="c-faq-item">
          <h3>Does Wolvec publish pricing?</h3>
          <p>Wolvec does not currently publish pricing. Wolvec is in early access by invitation.</p>
        </div>
        </div>
      </section>

